-- Text as the page shows it (language.md §11.4, frontend.md §9.7): lines
-- trimmed and joined, whitespace collapsed, then character references
-- decoded — so `&nbsp;` survives as U+00A0 and a typed U+00A0 collapses
-- like a space; the longest name wins (`&notit;` is `¬it;`) and U+0080
-- maps through windows-1252 (`&#x80;` is `€`); a run of only whitespace is
-- no node. A quoted value decodes its literal text, chunk by chunk around
-- an interpolation, but not what an escape produces (`\u{26}amp;`); a
-- hole's string is never decoded.
view x =
    <p title="Fish &amp; chips" class="a &lt; ${x} &gt;" lang="\u{26}amp;">
        Hello,&nbsp;world   and  more
        &notit; &#x80; AT&T  space
        <b>{"&amp;"}</b> <i>x</i>
    </p>
